English

Personal Information Protection and Rights of the Personal Data Subject

App name: Nested Folders
Developer name: igoivo
Distribution channel: Huawei AppGallery
Last updated: September 8, 2026

1. Personal information collection

Nested Folders (by igoivo) does not collect personal information for the developer, does not create user accounts, and does not send personal information to the developer or to any external server.

The application reads the list of launcher applications installed on the user's device only to provide its core local function: displaying installed applications and organizing them into folders and subfolders. This installed-application list is processed locally on the user's phone only.

2. Necessary scope

The application follows the data minimization principle. The scope is limited to data needed for local app-icon organization:

- installed application names and package/component identifiers;
- folder and subfolder names created by the user;
- app-to-folder assignments selected or generated on the device;
- local settings and local display cache;
- XML backup files created or imported by the user in a user-selected folder.

The application does not collect contacts, SMS, call records, photos, precise location, microphone data, camera data, account data, payment data, health data, biometric data, browsing records, search records, or advertising identifiers.

3. Use of personal information

The locally processed installed-application list is used only for local cataloging, organizing, restoring, and displaying the user's app-folder layout. It is not used for profiling, advertising, marketing, targeted push notifications, precision recommendations, credit evaluation, risk scoring, or any unrelated purpose.

4. Targeted push notifications and precision advertising

The application does not provide targeted push notifications, precision advertising, personalized marketing, advertising recommendations, or analytics-based recommendations. Therefore, the application does not use personal information for such functions and does not include an option for targeted-push personalization.

5. Permissions and access behavior

The application does not request network access and does not upload user data. It does not request broad sensitive permissions such as contacts, SMS, call log, location, microphone, camera, phone state, or account access.

The application has limited access only to a backup folder selected by the user, and only for creating or reading XML backup files. The user can stop this local access by clearing application data, deleting backup files, changing system permissions where available, or uninstalling the application.

6. Automatic launch and secondary launch

The application does not automatically launch other applications for data collection. When the user chooses to open an installed application or a market page, that action is initiated by the user and is part of normal app navigation.

7. Sharing, transfer, and third-party processing

The application does not share, transfer, sell, disclose, or upload user data. It does not include advertising SDKs, analytics SDKs, tracking SDKs, or third-party personal-data collection services.

8. Rights of the personal data subject

Because the developer does not receive or store user personal information on any server, the developer cannot remotely access, correct, copy, export, restrict, or delete such data. The user controls the local data directly on the device.

The user may exercise rights related to local data by deleting local backup files, clearing application data in Android system settings, managing permissions where available, or uninstalling the application.

If applicable law treats the locally processed installed-application list as personal information, these rights are still exercised locally because the list is not transferred outside the user's phone.

